======================================================================
CORRECTED NEAR-TRANSITIVE CONSTRUCTION
======================================================================

Construction: Start with total order σ = (v₁ > v₂ > ... > vₙ).
Reverse the SINGLE arc from vₙ (min) to v₁ (max).
Result: vₙ → v₁ (instead of v₁ → vₙ), all other arcs unchanged.

This creates exactly n-2 directed 3-cycles: {v₁, vₖ, vₙ} for k=2,...,n-1.
Each cycle: vₙ → v₁ → vₖ → vₙ (since v₁ beats vₖ and vₖ beats vₙ).

n=3: H=3, c3=1, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=False, expected H=3
n=4: H=5, c3=2, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=True, expected H=5
n=5: H=9, c3=3, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=True, expected H=9
n=6: H=17, c3=4, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=True, expected H=17
n=7: H=33, c3=5, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=True, expected H=33
n=8: H=?, c3=6, is_DAG=True, is_total_order=True, expected H=65

